      "id": "T-RENDERER",
      "title": "Task rows and diagnosis parsing",
      "objective": "Extend src/boardscan.py KEEPING the existing load_projects unchanged. Add format_task_row(task: dict) -> str rendering one task as columns [id, TITLE, STATUS, ATTEMPTS, DEPS] joined by ' | ': id and title have \n and \r replaced by spaces; STATUS is the task status verbatim when it is one of done|pending|failed else '?'; ATTEMPTS is str(task.get('retry_count', 0)); DEPS is ', '.join(dependencies) or '-' when empty/missing. Add parse_diagnosis(feedback: str | None) -> dict | None: only feedback that starts with 'DIAGNOSIS:' AND matches 'DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<confidence>) remedy=<remedy>' returns {'cause': str, 'confidence': str, 'remedy': str} (confidence is the raw token after 'confidence='); anything else, including None and 'DIAGNOSIS:' text without the grammar, returns None. Add render_table(projects: list) -> str consuming load_projects' output: skip (name, exception) tuples silently; for each readable board emit header '== <name> ==', one format_task_row line per task in board['tasks'] order (a board without a tasks list renders the header only), then one indented line '  DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<confidence>) remedy=<remedy>' per task whose parse_diagnosis is not None; join all lines with '\n' and no trailing newline; empty input returns ''. Do not change earlier functions.",
